cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "darkfiber: a physics-first coherence engine for Distributed Acoustic Sensing"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-20"
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sirkraven/darkfiber"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21383276
authors:
  - family-names: "Yucare Rios"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
    alias: "Sirkraven"
keywords:
  - distributed-acoustic-sensing
  - seismology
  - earthquake-detection
  - fiber-optic-sensing
  - phased-array
  - das
abstract: >
  darkfiber classifies events recorded on Distributed Acoustic Sensing (DAS)
  fiber-optic arrays by measuring the physics of how they propagate across
  the array (slant-stack semblance, coincidence, trajectory regression)
  rather than treating each channel as an independent classification
  problem. Validated on both synthetic scenarios with known ground truth
  and real earthquake recordings (Stanford DAS array, QuakeFlow DAS
  dataset), with a public ledger tying every real-data verdict to its
  USGS-published origin.
